 "気": "رُوح (The soul of a person or other creature.) / رُوَح (A supernatural being, often but not exclusively without physical form; ghost, fa) / كُحُول (A volatile liquid, such as alcohol. The plural form spirits is a generic term fo)  [spirit]\nمثال: 彼は年はとっているが気は若い。\n→ Though he is old, he has a youthful spirit. / طَبِيعَة, طبيعة (The way things are, the totality of all things in the physical universe and thei)  [nature]\nمثال: 彼は親切というよりむしろ気がやさしい。\n→ He is more gentle than kind. / قَصْد, إِرَادَة (A course of action that a person intends to follow.)  [intention]\noft. after a verb\nمثال: もう待つ気が無くなった。\n→ I don't feel like waiting any longer. / مَزَاج (A sullen, gloomy or angry mental state; a bad mood.)  [mood]\nمثال: 人に褒められて悪い気はしない。\n→ No one feels displeased when he is praised.",
 "気がかり": "قَلِقَ (To be troubled; to give way to mental anxiety or doubt.) / قَلَق (A strong feeling of anxiety.)  [worry]\nمثال: 私は将来のことが気がかりだ。\n→ I am anxious about the future.",
 "気がする": "تحسس (To use or experience the sense of touch.) / شَعَرَ (To sense or think emotionally or judgmentally.) / شَعَرَ بِ (To sense or think emotionally or judgmentally.)  [to feel (as if)] / [to feel like doing ; to want to do]\nafter a verb; usu. in the negative",
 "気がつく": "لَاحَظَ (To remark upon; to mention.) / لَاحَظَ, اِنْتَبَهَ (To become aware of; to observe.)  [to notice]\nمثال: ドアを閉めてから、鍵を置いてきたことに気がついた。\n→ After I shut the door, I remembered I had left my key behind. / [to be attentive ; to be scrupulous]\nمثال: 何時間もたって彼は気がついた。\n→ It was many hours before he came to. / [to regain consciousness ; to come to (one's senses)]",
 "気がつくと": "فَجْأَةً (Suddenly, quickly, without warning.)  [all of a sudden]",
 "気がもめる": "قَلِقَ (To be troubled; to give way to mental anxiety or doubt.) / قَلَق (A strong feeling of anxiety.)  [to worry]",
 "気が付く": "لَاحَظَ (To remark upon; to mention.) / لَاحَظَ, اِنْتَبَهَ (To become aware of; to observe.)  [to notice]\nمثال: ドアを閉めてから、鍵を置いてきたことに気がついた。\n→ After I shut the door, I remembered I had left my key behind. / [to be attentive ; to be scrupulous]\nمثال: 何時間もたって彼は気がついた。\n→ It was many hours before he came to. / [to regain consciousness ; to come to (one's senses)]",
 "気が付くと": "فَجْأَةً (Suddenly, quickly, without warning.)  [all of a sudden]",
 "気が変": "مَجْنُون, مَخْبُول (Exhibiting unsoundness or disorder of mind; not sane; utterly mad.)  [insane]",
 "気が変わる": "غَيَّرَ رَأْيَهُ (To decide differently than one had decided before.)  [to change one's mind]\nمثال: なぜ彼は気が変わったのか。\n→ What made him change his mind?",
 "気が多い": "مُتَقَلِّب (Impulsive and unpredictable; determined by chance, impulse, or whim.)  [capricious]",
 "気が大きい": "كَرِيم (Willing to give and share unsparingly; showing a readiness to give more (especia)  [generous]\nمثال: 海外に行くと、気が大きくなって思わず使いすぎちゃうんだよね。\n→ When you travel abroad, you start to feel very expansive, and it's easy to overspend in a mood like that.",
 "気が小さい": "جَبَان (Lacking in courage or confidence.)  [timid]",
 "気が差す": "قَلِقَ (To be troubled; to give way to mental anxiety or doubt.) / قَلَق (A strong feeling of anxiety.)  [to worry (about something)]",
 "気が弱い": "جَبَان (Lacking in courage or confidence.)  [timid]",
 "気が抜ける": "يَئِسَ, أُحْبِطَ (To despair; to experience reduced morale; to become disheartened.)  [to lose heart] / [to become stale (i.e. of a carbonated beverage) ; to go flat]\nمثال: 気が抜けないうちにビールを飲んで下さい。\n→ Please drink the beer before it goes flat. / [to lose focus ; to let one's guard down]",
 "気が揉める": "قَلِقَ (To be troubled; to give way to mental anxiety or doubt.) / قَلَق (A strong feeling of anxiety.)  [to worry]",
