 "気が置かれる": "[to feel constraint ; to feel uneasy] / قَلِقَ (To be troubled; to give way to mental anxiety or doubt.) / قَلَق (A strong feeling of anxiety.)  [to worry]",
 "気が荒い": "عُدْوَانِيّ (tending or disposed to aggress) / هُجُومِيّ (tending or disposed to aggress)  [aggressive]",
 "気が軽い": "مُرْتَاحُ اَلْبَالِ, خَالِي اَلْقَلْبِ (Without cares or worries; free of concern or worries; without difficulty.)  [carefree]",
 "気が遠くなる": "إِغْمَاء (The act of fainting, syncope.) / أُغْمِيَ, غُشِيَ (To lose consciousness through a lack of oxygen or nutrients to the brain, usuall)  [to faint]\nمثال: 彼女の恐怖は非常なものだったので気が遠くなるところだった。\n→ She was on the verge of fainting out of sheer terror. / [to be in a daze ; to feel overwhelmed]\nمثال: それは気が遠くなるような計画だ。\n→ It is a stupendous project.",
 "気が重い": "مُحْبَط, مُكْتَئِب (Unhappy; despondent.)  [depressed]\nمثال: やらなくてはならないことが多かったので、私は気が重い。\n→ I feel depressed because there were a lot of things I had to do.",
 "気が長い": "صَبُور (Willing to wait if necessary; not losing one's temper while waiting.) / مَرِيض, مَرِيضَة (A person or animal that receives health care from a doctor, nurse, dentist, alli) / مَفْعُول (The noun or noun phrase that is semantically on the receiving end of a verb's ac)  [patient]",
 "気さく": "لَطِيف (Generally warm, approachable and easy to relate with in character.)  [friendly]\nمثال: ある意味では、丁寧語は気さくな雰囲気を壊す。\n→ Polite language, in a sense, spoils a casual atmosphere.",
