 "決まり悪い": "مُحْرَج, بِٱلْحَرَج (Having a feeling of shameful discomfort.)  [embarrassed]",
 "決まる": "[to be decided ; to be settled]\nمثال: いつ始めるのかはまだ決まっていない。\n→ It is still undecided when we will begin. / [to be unchanging ; to be the same (as always)]\nas 決まっている or 決まった / [to be a fixed rule ; to be destined]\nas ...と決まっている / نَجَحَ (To prevail in obtaining an intended objective or accomplishment; to prosper as a)  [to succeed]",
 "決め": "اِتِّفَاق, تَوَافُق (An understanding between entities to follow a specific course of conduct.) / إِقْرَار (A state whereby several parties share a view or opinion; the state of not contra) / اِتِّفَاق, اِتِّفَاقِيَّة (A legally binding contract enforceable in a court of law.)  [agreement]",
 "決めうち": "دَرِيئَة, نِيشَان (A butt or mark to shoot at, as for practice, or to test the accuracy of a firear) / هَدَف, مَرْمًى (A goal or objective.) / يَسْتَهْدِفُ (To aim something, especially a weapon, at (a target).)  [targeting] / [selective hitting ; swinging only at certain types of pitches] / [having no choice in a move (in mahjong, go, etc.)]",
 "決めこむ": "سلّم جدلا (To assume something to be true without verification or proof.)  [to take for granted] / اِدَّعَى (1. (intransitive or with 'that' clause or 'to' infinitive) T) / زَعَمَ (1. (intransitive or with 'that' clause or 'to' infinitive) T) / تَظَاهَرَ (1. (intransitive or with 'that' clause or 'to' infinitive) T)  [to pretend (to be)]\nمثال: 本人は唯我独尊を決め込んでいるようだけども、周りから見れば単なるわがままだよね。\n→ He's completely convinced of his own greatness but to the people around him he's just a selfish jerk. / وَطَّنَ نَفْسَهُ عَلَى, عَزَمَ (To decide; to reach a conclusion.)  [to make up one's mind]\nمثال: 私は、議論が終わるのを辛抱強く待つことに決め込んだ。\n→ I decided to bide my time and wait for the argument to finish.",
 "決めつける": "[to fix upon (one-sidedly) ; to (ignore someone's position and) arbitrarily decide something is the case]\nمثال: そういうの、先入観っていうんだよっ！体験したこと無いのに、決め付けるのはよくないっ！\n→ That's what they call 'prejudice'! It's wrong to make your mind up on something you've never experienced! / اِمْرَأَة سَلِيطَة (A person who habitually scolds, in particular a troublesome and angry woman.) / وَبَّخَ (To rebuke angrily.)  [to scold]\nمثال: 上司は僕の仕事振りがいい加減だと決め付けた。\n→ My boss took me to task for the poor quality of my work.",
 "決める": "قَرَّرَ, صَمَّمَ (To resolve (a contest, problem, dispute, etc.); to choose, determine, or settle.) / قَرَّرَ (To make a judgment, especially after deliberation.)  [to decide]\nمثال: そこに行くことに決めた。\n→ I made up my mind to go there. / قَرَّرَ, صَمَّمَ (To resolve (a contest, problem, dispute, etc.); to choose, determine, or settle.) / قَرَّرَ (To make a judgment, especially after deliberation.)  [to decide (the outcome of a match)] / [to persist in doing ; to go through with] / [to always do ; to have made a habit of]\nas 決めている",
 "決め付ける": "[to fix upon (one-sidedly) ; to (ignore someone's position and) arbitrarily decide something is the case]\nمثال: そういうの、先入観っていうんだよっ！体験したこと無いのに、決め付けるのはよくないっ！\n→ That's what they call 'prejudice'! It's wrong to make your mind up on something you've never experienced! / اِمْرَأَة سَلِيطَة (A person who habitually scolds, in particular a troublesome and angry woman.) / وَبَّخَ (To rebuke angrily.)  [to scold]\nمثال: 上司は僕の仕事振りがいい加減だと決め付けた。\n→ My boss took me to task for the poor quality of my work.",
