 "泣きしきる": "بَكَى, عَيَّط (To shed tears; to weep, especially in anger or sadness.) / صَاحَ (To shout, scream, yell.) / بكاء (A shedding of tears; the act of crying.)  [to cry]",
 "泣きじゃくる": "شهيق, شهقة (A cry with a short, sudden expulsion of breath.) / شَهِقَ (To weep with convulsive gasps.)  [to sob]\nمثال: 寝室に入るや否や、彼女は泣きじゃくり出した。\n→ On entering the bedroom, she started sobbing.",
 "泣きつく": "اِلْتِمَاس, اِسْتِئْنَاف (An application to a superior court or judge for a decision or order by an inferi) / اِسْتَأْنَفَ ((intransitive) to apply to a superior court or judge for a d)  [to appeal]\nمثال: 案の定、あの業者今日になって泣きついてきたよ。\n→ Just like I thought, the contractor came back today, begging for more time.",
 "泣きまね": "دُمُوع اَلتَّمَاسِيح (A display of tears that is forced or false.)  [crocodile tears]",
 "泣きわめく": "صَيح, صِيَاح (A loud burst of voice or voices; a violent and sudden outcry, especially that of) / صَرَخَ, صَاحَ (To utter a sudden and loud cry, as in joy, triumph, exultation or anger, or to a)  [to shout (while crying)]\nمثال: 子供はおもちゃの車が欲しいと泣きわめいた。\n→ The child cried for a toy car.",
 "泣き付く": "اِلْتِمَاس, اِسْتِئْنَاف (An application to a superior court or judge for a decision or order by an inferi) / اِسْتَأْنَفَ ((intransitive) to apply to a superior court or judge for a d)  [to appeal]\nمثال: 案の定、あの業者今日になって泣きついてきたよ。\n→ Just like I thought, the contractor came back today, begging for more time.",
