 "泣き叫ぶ": "صرخة (A loud, emphatic, exclamation of extreme emotion, especially horror, fear, excit) / صَرَخَ (to make the sound of a scream)  [to scream]\nمثال: 幼児はしゃべることができないので、ほしいものが手に入るまで泣き叫ぶ。\n→ An infant is not capable of speaking, so it just screams until it gets what it wants.",
 "泣き喚く": "صَيح, صِيَاح (A loud burst of voice or voices; a violent and sudden outcry, especially that of) / صَرَخَ, صَاحَ (To utter a sudden and loud cry, as in joy, triumph, exultation or anger, or to a)  [to shout (while crying)]\nمثال: 子供はおもちゃの車が欲しいと泣きわめいた。\n→ The child cried for a toy car.",
 "泣き声": "بَكَى, عَيَّط (To shed tears; to weep, especially in anger or sadness.) / صَاحَ (To shout, scream, yell.) / بكاء (A shedding of tears; the act of crying.)  [cry (e.g. of a baby)]\nمثال: 病気の子どもの痛ましい泣き声を聞くのは我々には耐えられなかった。\n→ We could not bear to listen to the sick child's pathetic cries. / [tearful voice ; weepy voice]",
