 "泣き立てる": "عُوَاء (The protracted, mournful cry of a dog, wolf or other canid; also of other animal) / عَوَى (To utter a loud, protracted, mournful sound or cry, as dogs and wolves often do.) / أَنَّ (To utter a sound expressive of pain or distress; to cry aloud and mournfully; to)  [to howl]",
 "泣き言": "شِكَايَة, شَكْوَى (A grievance, problem, difficulty, or concern.)  [complaint]\nمثال: 人は泣きつつ生まれ、泣き言を言いつつ暮らし、失望落胆して死ぬ。\n→ We are born crying, spend our lives complaining, and die disappointed.",
 "泣き頻る": "بَكَى, عَيَّط (To shed tears; to weep, especially in anger or sadness.) / صَاحَ (To shout, scream, yell.) / بكاء (A shedding of tears; the act of crying.)  [to cry]",
 "泣く": "بَكَى, عَيَّط (To shed tears; to weep, especially in anger or sadness.) / صَاحَ (To shout, scream, yell.) / بكاء (A shedding of tears; the act of crying.)  [to cry]\nمثال: ビルは何時間も泣き続けた。\n→ Bill kept on crying for hours. / تَأَلَّمَ, عَانَى (To undergo hardship.) / عَانَى (To endure, undergo.)  [to suffer (from)]\nusu. as ...に泣く / قَبِلَ (To receive, especially with a consent, with favour, or with approval.) / اِعْتَرَفَ (To admit to a place or a group.) / قَبِلَ (To receive or admit to; to agree to; to assent to; to submit to.)  [to accept (an unreasonable request, loss, etc.)] / تَأَلَّمَ, عَانَى (To undergo hardship.) / عَانَى (To endure, undergo.)  [to suffer (of a reputation)]",
