 "注": "تَعْلِيق, مَلْحُوظَة (A spoken or written remark.) / عَلَّقَ (To remark.)  [comment]\nمثال: 注はページの下欄についている。\n→ The notes are at the bottom of the page.",
 "注ぐ": "صَبَّ, سَكَبَ (To cause (liquid, or liquid-like substance) to flow in a stream, either out of a)  [to pour (into)]\nمثال: 私はビニール袋にワインを注ぎ、それからそれを氷水に付けた。\n→ I poured the wine in a plastic bag and then dipped it in ice water. / مِيَاه (A body of water, almost always a river, sometimes a lake or reservoir, especiall) / سَقَى (To wet or supply with water; to moisten; to overflow with water; to irrigate.) / أَسْقَى, سَقَى (To wet or supply with water; to moisten; to overflow with water; to irrigate.)  [to water (e.g. plants)] / سَقِيفَة (temporary structure to shelter something)  [to shed (tears)]\nas 涙を〜 / [to concentrate one's energy (strength, attention, etc.) on ; to devote to]\nمثال: 彼は友人を助けることに全力を注いだ。\n→ He concentrated his energies on helping his friend.",
 "注す": "صَبَّ, سَكَبَ (To cause (liquid, or liquid-like substance) to flow in a stream, either out of a)  [to pour]\nesp. 注す / لَبِسَ, اِرْتَدَى (To don (clothing, equipment, or the like).)  [to put on (lipstick, etc.)]\nesp. 点す",
 "注入": "صَبَّ, سَكَبَ (To cause (liquid, or liquid-like substance) to flow in a stream, either out of a)  [pouring]\nمثال: この緊急な事態において、人事や制度を改革し、清新な雰囲気と新しい観念を、われわれの組織の中に注入する以外に方策はない。\n→ We have no other alternative but to swap horses midstream and inject a fresh atmosphere and new ideas into our organization.",
 "注射": "حُقْنَة, حَقْن (The act of injecting, or something that is injected.)  [injection]\nمثال: 流感の予防ワクチンの注射をした。\n→ I was vaccinated against the flu.",
