 "流れる": "جَدْوَل (A small river; a large creek; a body of moving water confined by banks.) / تَيَّار (Any steady flow or succession of material, such as water, air, radio signal or w) / تَدَفّقَ (To flow in a continuous or steady manner, like a liquid.)  [to stream]\nمثال: アルフォンスが空を見上げたまま、速く流れる雲を見つめていた。\n→ Alphonse looked at the racing clouds, his eyes turned to the sky. / [to be washed away ; to be carried]\nمثال: 当時はきれいな水がこの川にも流れていた。\n→ Pure water was washed away to this river as well at that time. / طَفَا, عَامَ (To be supported by a fluid of greater density (than the object).) / طَفَا (To be capable of floating.)  [to float (e.g. clouds)] / مَسَحَ (To clean (a surface) by means of a stroking motion of a broom or brush.)  [to sweep (e.g. rumour, fire)]\nمثال: ジャネットとデイブがあやしいという噂が流れた。\n→ Word got around that Jeanette and Dave were having an affair.",
