 "湯煮": "غَلَيَان (The process of changing the state of a substance from liquid to gas by heating i)  [boiling (e.g. food)]",
 "湯舟": "بَانْيُو, مَغْسَل (A large container for holding water in which a person may bathe (take a bath).)  [bathtub] / [boat with a bathtub rented to customers (Edo period)]",
 "湯船": "بَانْيُو, مَغْسَل (A large container for holding water in which a person may bathe (take a bath).)  [bathtub] / [boat with a bathtub rented to customers (Edo period)]",
 "湾": "خَلِيج, شَرْم (A body of water (especially the sea) contained by a concave shoreline.)  [bay]\nمثال: 川は山から下って湾に注いでいる。\n→ The river descends from the mountains to the bay below.",
 "湾岸危機": "حَرْب الْخَلِيج الثَّانِيَة (One of several wars fought at the Persian Gulf in the 1980s, 1990s, 2000s)  [Gulf War (1990)]",
 "湾岸戦争": "حَرْب الْخَلِيج الثَّانِيَة (One of several wars fought at the Persian Gulf in the 1980s, 1990s, 2000s)  [Gulf War (1990-1991)]\nمثال: １９９０年代は湾岸戦争で始まった。\n→ The 1990s began with the Gulf War.",
 "湾岸紛争": "حَرْب الْخَلِيج الثَّانِيَة (One of several wars fought at the Persian Gulf in the 1980s, 1990s, 2000s)  [Gulf War (1990)]\nمثال: １９９０年代は湾岸紛争で始まった。\n→ The 1990s began with the Gulf incident.",
 "湾曲": "منحنى (A bend, such as in a road.)  [curve]\nمثال: 城からそのふもとをゆるやかに湾曲して流れる川全体が見えました。\n→ From the castle we could see the whole curve of the river around its base.",
 "湾曲部": "ثَنَى (to cause to shape into a curve)  [bend] / [bight]",
 "湾流": "تَيَّار الْخَلِيج (The warm ocean current issuing from the Gulf of Mexico, flowing northeastwards a)  [the Gulf Stream]",
 "湿": "رُطُوبَة (The state of being moist.)  [moisture] / جَرَب (An infestation of parasitic mites, Sarcoptes scabiei, causing intense itching ca)  [scabies]",
 "湿す": "مُبْتَلّ (Made up of liquid or moisture, usually (but not always) water.) / مَبْلُول, مُبْتَلّ (Of an object, etc.: covered or impregnated with liquid, usually (but not always))  [to wet]",
 "湿っぽい": "رُطُوبة (Moisture; humidity; dampness.)  [damp]\nمثال: このシーツ、湿っぽいよ。\n→ The sheets feel damp. / كَئِيب, مُوحِش (Suffering from gloom; melancholy; dejected.)  [gloomy]",
 "湿り": "رُطُوبَة (Dampness, especially that of the air.) / رُطُوبَة (The amount of water vapour in the air.)  [humidity]",
 "湿り気": "رُطُوبَة (The state of being moist.)  [moisture]\nمثال: 雨が降って土に湿り気があると草は取りやすくなる。\n→ When rain's fallen and the soil is moist, it becomes easier to pull out weeds.",
 "湿地": "مستنقع (Chicken bog.)  [bog]",
 "湿布": "لَبْخَة (A soft, moist mass, usually wrapped in cloth and warmed, that is applied topical)  [poultice]\nمثال: ２時間毎に局部を湿布しなさい。\n→ Apply a compress to the affected part every two hours.",
 "湿布薬": "لَبْخَة (A soft, moist mass, usually wrapped in cloth and warmed, that is applied topical)  [poultice]",
 "湿度": "رُطُوبَة (Dampness, especially that of the air.) / رُطُوبَة (The amount of water vapour in the air.)  [humidity]\nمثال: ニューヨークの天候は、夏は暑く湿度も高い。\n→ New York weather is hot and humid in the summer.",
