 "満": "[being full] / [(counting) completed years (e.g. when calculating age)] / مُمْتَلِئ, مَلِيء (Containing the maximum possible amount that can fit in the space available.) / شِبَع, شبعان (Having the attention, thoughts, etc., absorbed in any matter, and the feelings m)  [full (years, months, etc.)]\nbefore a number / مَنْشُورِيَا (Synonym of Manchukuo: a former puppet state of Imperial Japan.)  [Manchuria]",
 "満たざる": "أَصْغَر مِن, صُغْرَى مِن (The character <, used to show that one amount or number is smaller than another.)  [less than]\nusu. に満たない, etc.\nمثال: 風土病に対する予防接種を受けていたのは１００人中１人にも満たないということが見出された。\n→ It was discovered that less than one child in a hundred had been inoculated against endemic disease.",
 "満たす": "رَضَّى (to be enough (for))  [to satisfy (conditions, one's appetite, etc.)]\nمثال: この仕事はわれわれの必要条件を満たしていない。\n→ This work does not meet our requirements. / مَلَأَ (To make full)  [to fill (e.g. a cup)]\nمثال: このコップをミルクで満たした。\n→ I filled this glass with milk.",
 "満たない": "أَصْغَر مِن, صُغْرَى مِن (The character <, used to show that one amount or number is smaller than another.)  [less than]\nusu. に満たない, etc.\nمثال: 風土病に対する予防接種を受けていたのは１００人中１人にも満たないということが見出された。\n→ It was discovered that less than one child in a hundred had been inoculated against endemic disease.",
 "満ちる": "مَلَأَ (To make full)  [to fill]\nمثال: 「世界平和」という言葉は魅力的に聞こえるが、世界平和への道は長く苦難に満ちている。\n→ Although the phrase \"world peace\" sounds attractive, the road to world peace is very long and full of troubles. / شَمْع, شَمَع (Any oily, water-resistant, solid or semisolid substance; normally long-chain hyd)  [to wax (of the moon)] / نَهَضَ, اِرْتَفْعَ (To move, or appear to move, physically upwards relative to the ground.) / أَشْرَقَ, شَرَقَ (To move, or appear to move, physically upwards relative to the ground.)  [to rise (of the tide)]\nمثال: 潮が急速に満ちてくる。\n→ The tide is rising fast. / نَاضِج, رَاشِد (Fully developed; grown up in terms of physical appearance, behaviour or thinking) / نَاضِج (To attain maturity, to become mature or ripe.)  [to mature]",
 "満ち足りる": "[to be content ; to have enough]\nمثال: 満ち足りた心は永遠の祝宴である。\n→ A contented mind is a perpetual feast. / نَهَضَ, اِرْتَفْعَ (To move, or appear to move, physically upwards relative to the ground.) / أَشْرَقَ, شَرَقَ (To move, or appear to move, physically upwards relative to the ground.)  [to rise (of the tide)]",
 "満つ": "[to be full]\nusu. as 〜に満たない / شَمْع, شَمَع (Any oily, water-resistant, solid or semisolid substance; normally long-chain hyd)  [to wax (e.g. moon)] / نَهَضَ, اِرْتَفْعَ (To move, or appear to move, physically upwards relative to the ground.) / أَشْرَقَ, شَرَقَ (To move, or appear to move, physically upwards relative to the ground.)  [to rise (e.g. tide)] / نَاضِج, رَاشِد (Fully developed; grown up in terms of physical appearance, behaviour or thinking) / نَاضِج (To attain maturity, to become mature or ripe.)  [to mature]",
