 "焙る": "دَافِئ (having a temperature slightly higher than usual) / دَفِيء (having a temperature slightly higher than usual)  [to warm (e.g. one's hands over a fire)]\nمثال: 彼は濡れた服を火にあぶってかわかした。\n→ He dried his wet clothes by the fire. / شواية (A grating; a grid of wire or a sheet of material with a pattern of holes or slot) / مُصَبَّع (On a vehicle, a slotted cover as above, to protect and hide the radiator, while ) / مِشْوَاة (A cooking device comprising a source of radiative heat and a means of holding fo) / شِوَاء (A cooking device comprising a source of radiative and convective heat and a mean) / مَشْوِيَّات (Food (designed to be) cooked on a grill.) / شَوَى, يَشْوِي (To cook (food) on a grill; to barbecue.)  [to grill]\nمثال: それは油であぶられた。\n→ That was cooked in oil.",
