 "無": "لَا شَيْء (Not any thing; no thing.)  [nothing]\nمثال: 無から有は生じない。\n→ Nothing comes from nothing. / [un- ; non-]",
 "無い": "مَعْدُوم (Not existent or existing; not real.)  [nonexistent]\nمثال: ２つの意見に大した差はない。\n→ There is not much difference between the two opinions. / [unowned ; not had]\nمثال: 車も何もなく、生活保護で生きてます。\n→ I'm living on welfare, without a car or anything. / فَرِيد, فَذّ (Being the only one of its kind; unequaled, unparalleled or unmatched.)  [unique] / لَا, مَا (Negates the meaning of the modified verb.) / لَا (And not.)  [not]\nas ...ことがない, etc.; indicates negation, inexperience, unnecessariness or impossibility",
 "無いことには": "إِلَّا (Except on a specified condition; if not.)  [unless (you do something)]\nwith verb stem",
 "無い事には": "إِلَّا (Except on a specified condition; if not.)  [unless (you do something)]\nwith verb stem",
 "無い内に": "قَبْلَ (Earlier than (in time).) / قَبْلَ, أَمَامَ (In front of in space.) / قَبْلَ (In front of, according to a formal system of ordering items.)  [before (an undesirable thing occurs)]\nafter neg. stem of verb\nمثال: 私たちは暗くならないうちにテントを張った。\n→ We set up our tents before dark.",
