 "無かったことにする": "سَامَحَ ((''transitive'') to pardon) / غَفَرَ ((''transitive'') to pardon)  [to forgive (something)]",
 "無かった事にする": "سَامَحَ ((''transitive'') to pardon) / غَفَرَ ((''transitive'') to pardon)  [to forgive (something)]",
 "無き": "بِلَا, غَيْر ... (Lacking (something); without (something). Added usually to a noun to form an adj)  [-less]\nمثال: この遣り場なき怒りをどこにぶつければいいのか。\n→ Where can I find an outlet for all my anger?",
 "無くして": "بِدُونِ, بِلَا (Not having, containing, characteristic of, etc.)  [without]\nمثال: 労なくして益なし。\n→ No pain, no gain.",
 "無くしては": "بِدُونِ, بِلَا (Not having, containing, characteristic of, etc.)  [without]\nمثال: この食べ物は、それなくしては我々の身体が正しく機能しないすべてのミネラルを含んでいます。\n→ This food contains all the minerals without which our bodies would not function.",
 "無くす": "فَقَدَ (To cease to have (something) in one's possession or capability.) / خَسِرَ (To become a defeated competitor in (a game, competition, trial, etc).) / خَسِرَ (To be defeated (in a game, competition, contest, etc.))  [to lose (something)]\nمثال: 彼女は新しい時計をなくした。\n→ She lost her new watch. / تَخَلَّصَ ... مِن (To rid oneself of; to cause oneself to be free of or released from.)  [to get rid of]\nمثال: その国の財政の赤字をなくすには、もっと、たくさんの外国の援助を注ぎ込まなければならなかった。\n→ To get the nation's economy out of the red, more foreign aid had to be pumped in.",
 "無くちゃ": "بِدُونِ, بِلَا (Not having, containing, characteristic of, etc.)  [without] / [have to do]\nafter negative stem of verb\nمثال: 試験勉強をしなくちゃ。\n→ I have to prepare for the test.",
 "無くては": "بِدُونِ, بِلَا (Not having, containing, characteristic of, etc.)  [without] / [have to do]\nafter negative stem of verb\nمثال: 試験勉強をしなくちゃ。\n→ I have to prepare for the test.",
 "無くても良い": "يَضْطَر (Must; need to; to be urged to; to be required to; indicates obligation.)  [(not) have to]\nafter neg. stem of verb or adjective, expressing absence of obligation or necessity\nمثال: わざわざ彼を訪ねて行かなくてもよい。\n→ Don't bother to call on him. / [need not have ; need not exist]\nمثال: あなたは明日、車がなくてもいいかしら。私、車が必要なの。\n→ Can you do without the car tomorrow? I need it.",
 "無くなす": "فَقَدَ (To cease to have (something) in one's possession or capability.) / خَسِرَ (To become a defeated competitor in (a game, competition, trial, etc).) / خَسِرَ (To be defeated (in a game, competition, contest, etc.))  [to lose (something)]",
 "無くなる": "[to be lost (e.g. luggage) ; to be missing]\nمثال: それで疑いをさしはさむ余地はなくなる。\n→ That leaves no room for doubt. / [to be used up ; to be run out]\nمثال: 残り時間があまりなくなってきた。\n→ The sands are running out. / اِخْتَفَى (To vanish.) / أَخْفَى (To make vanish; especially, to abduct or murder for political reasons.)  [to disappear (e.g. pain)]\nمثال: やがてこの世から戦争がなくなる日がくるだろう。\n→ The day will soon come when there will be no more wars in the world.",
 "無くもがな": "عَدِيمُ الْفَائِدَةِ (Without use or the possibility to be used.)  [useless]",
 "無さそう": "مِنْ غَيْرِ المُرَجَّحِ (Not likely; improbable; not to be reasonably expected.)  [unlikely]\nمثال: 「宝くじでも買う？」「俺、ギャンブル運とか無さそうだしなぁ」\n→ \"Buy a lottery ticket or something?\" \"Well, I don't think I've got much luck with gambling.\"",
